    "narrative": "The clear centerpiece for today\u2019s lineup is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts a dominant 76.07 score. His matchup against T. Gordon is favorable, but the real catalyst is the 14% park factor boost coupled with a rare \"Slow SP Delivery\" designation that signals high potential for a stolen base\u2014a critical asset given our aggressive pursuit of the SB category. Joining him at the top of the board are **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Lawrence Butler** (68.16), both benefiting from significant platoon advantages and neutral-to-hitter-friendly environments. **Bryce Harper** remains a steady anchor at 67.36, as his elite xwOBA metrics continue to provide a high floor even against a competent arm like Dobbins.\n\nTactical adjustments highlight **JJ Bleday** and **Gleyber Torres** as high-value plays today. **JJ Bleday** climbs to a 66.17 score thanks to a massive 16% SP skill benefit and a platoon edge against E-Rod, while **Gleyber Torres** receives a substantial 13% boost from his favorable matchup against a left-handed starter. On the fringe, **Zack Gelof** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his 55.18 score is respectable, he was ultimately benched because his platoon profile against the right-handed Wesneski lacks the ceiling provided by our outfield starters like **Daulton Varsho**, who is well-positioned for a productive outing.\n\nWe are monitoring the status of several bench assets, with **Tyler Freeman** and **Will Smith** currently unavailable due to IL designations, and **Jonathan Aranda** sitting outside the active rotation. While we are confident in our current construction, **Brendan Donovan** represents our lowest-scored starter at 47.78; he remains in the lineup primarily for his leadoff role and plate appearance volume, despite a challenging platoon split that currently suppresses his efficiency. We have sufficient depth, but owners should keep an eye on weather reports, as any late-breaking conditions could impact the high-ceiling outlook for our primary power bats.",
